<article class="env-definition" id="0H3P">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H3P">Definition <span data-tag="0H3P">29.56.6</span>.</a> Let $f : Y \to X$ be a quasi-compact, quasi-separated, and dominant morphism of schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The factorization $Y \to X^{Y/sn} \to X$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0H3N" data-tag="0H3N">29.56.5</a> part (2) is the <em>seminormalization of $X$ in $Y$</em>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The factorization $Y \to X^{Y/wn} \to X$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/0H3N" data-tag="0H3N">29.56.5</a> part (1) is the <em>weak normalization of $X$ in $Y$</em>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>